proof.text:
Use the two equations from step 7 and cancel only the isomorphisms $\rho_{k_a}$. The common-dense-refinement descriptions in [det-sf-comp-coherence-cocycle] give
$$
\begin{aligned}
\phi_{c_2',c_1'}\beta_{c_1}
&=\rho_{k_2}^{-1}\rho_{k_1}\beta_{c_1}
=\rho_{k_2}^{-1}\rho_k\beta_dv^*\rho_{h_1}\\
&=\beta_{c_2}(v^*\rho_{h_2})^{-1}v^*\rho_{h_1}
=\beta_{c_2}v^*\phi_{c_2,c_1}.
\end{aligned}
$$
This is compatibility with arbitrary comparisons on both bases. The same cocycle makes it independent of the chosen $d,d''$ and allows comparison of $c_a'$ with any other compactification of $f'$. This proves (3).
